# The status file belongs to the running Pi, not to the source tree.
#
# It is written once a minute by pi-ui-status.timer into the web root, and
# modules/dashboard.sh deliberately excludes it from the rsync so a dashboard
# update leaves the live one alone. A copy in here is at best stale and at
# worst somebody's development machine described as a Raspberry Pi - which is
# exactly how one got committed during the 2.0.0 work.
apps/dashboard/build/status.json
apps/dashboard/public/status.json
